    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7054\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the granting of retirement service credit in the\noptional twenty year retirement plan to Duane A. Palma for service as a\ncorrection officer\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow the county of Monroe to offer an\noptional twenty-year retirement plan to Duane A. Palma.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one authorizes Monroe County to make participation in the\noptional twenty-year retirement plan as established by section 552 and\n553 of the retirement and social security law.\n\nSection two provides for the election of filing the request.\n\nSection three specifies that all costs associated with this act shall be\nborne by Monroe County.\n\nSection four sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDeputy Palma is currently employed with the Monroe County Sheriffs\nDepartment Road Patrol. He has of twenty years of law enforcement\nincluding agencies with the Rochester Police Department, Greece Police\nDepartment, as well as the Monroe County Sheriffs Office Jail Bureau.\nApproximately two years ago he transferred back to the Monroe Couhty\nSheriffs Department from the Greece Police Department informed that his\nprior Jail bureau service in the 89N retirement system was certified on\nthe front end of their retirement. Because other members of his employ-\nment tier have successfully used this time to retire, Deputy Palma\nanticipated it would apply in the future. For reasons not ascribable to\nhis own negligence, Deputy Palma was denied credit time for his service.\nThis bill allows Deputy Palma the option to join this retirement plan to\nrectify this error.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIf this bill is enacted during the 2025 Legislative Session, there will\nbe an immediate past service cost of approximately $160,000 which will\nbe borne by Monroe County as a one-time payment. This estimate assumes\nthat payment will be made on February 1, 2026. If Monroe County elects\nto amortize this cost over a five-year period, the cost for each year\nincluding interest would be $35,900.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
